{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Whoever kills Cain, vengeance shall be taken sevenfold.</b> I say to whoever is ready to kill Cain: I decree that the vengeance for his sin shall be seven doubled. For one who is ready to kill is called a killer, as it says: וְאֶפְרַיִם לְהוֹצִיא אֶל הוֹרֵג בָּנָיו (Hosea 9:13). And the word שִׁבְעָתַיִם teaches seven times two, like וְנִמְצָא יְשַׁלֵּם שִׁבְעָתָיִם (Proverbs 6:31). He decreed, then, that for this murder — which was the blood of his brother and half or a third of the human species — the vengeance shall be as for one who kills seven doubled in this manner: that the duration of six generations he shall be a wanderer and a fugitive, which is a life as bad as death or worse, as it says: אַל תַּהַרְגֵם פֶּן יִשְׁכְּחוּ עַמִּי הֲנִיעֵמוֹ בְחֵילְךָ (Psalms 59:12), and in the end he shall be killed in the seventh generation, as happened to him through Lemech, according to what is received in the tradition."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The phrase 'half or a third of the human species' refers to the premise that at that time only Adam, Eve, Cain, and Abel existed, so Abel's murder eliminated either half or a third of humanity depending on whether Eve is counted."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:37.752435881Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}